    {
      "id": "T-RENDERER",
      "title": "Task rows and diagnosis parsing",
      "objective": "src/boardscan.py ALREADY EXISTS. Its approved, gate-passed content is reproduced below between the markers. You must output the COMPLETE file: first reproduce the marked content EXACTLY (same function names, same signatures, same behavior -- this is what the previous task built and its tests pin), then append the new functions as specified after the markers. Do not rename or change anything in the marked part.\n---- BEGIN CURRENT CONTENT OF src/boardscan.py ----\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\n\ndef load_projects(root: str, project: str | None = None) -> list[tuple[str, object]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Load projects from <root>/projects/* (directories only, sorted ascending by name).\n    - If root is not an existing directory, raise SystemExit(2).\n    - If project is given and <root>/projects/<project> is not a directory, \n      print 'no such project: <project>' to stderr and raise SystemExit(2).\n    - Skip a project entirely when its .agent/task_board.json is missing.\n    - Return (name, parsed-board-dict) for readable boards and (name, exception) \n      for unreadable ones (JSONDecodeError/OSError).\n    \"\"\"\n    root_path = os.path.abspath(root) if root else \"\"\n    if not root or not os.path.isdir(root_path):\n        raise SystemExit(2)\n\n    projects_dir = os.path.join(root_path, \"projects\")\n\n    if project is not None:\n        proj_path = os.path.join(projects_dir, project)\n        if not os.path.isdir(proj_path):\n            sys.stderr.write(f\"no such project: {project}\\n\")\n            raise SystemExit(2)\n\n    if not os.path.isdir(projects_dir):\n        return []\n\n    try:\n        entries = sorted(\n            [e.name for e in os.scandir(projects_dir) if e.is_dir()],\n            key=lambda s: s\n        )\n    except OSError:\n        return []\n\n    if project is not None:\n        if project in entries:\n            entries = [project]\n        else:\n            entries = []\n\n    results: list[tuple[str, object]] = []\n\n    for name in entries:\n        board_path = os.path.join(projects_dir, name, \".agent\", \"task_board.json\")\n        if not os.path.isfile(board_path):\n            continue\n\n        try:\n            with open(board_path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n                data = json.load(f)\n            results.append((name, data))\n        except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError) as e:\n            results.append((name, e))\n\n    return results\n---- END CURRENT CONTENT OF src/boardscan.py ----\nNow ADD to the same file: format_task_row(task: dict) -> str rendering one task as columns [id, TITLE, STATUS, ATTEMPTS, DEPS] joined by ' | ': in id and in title, first replace every '\\r\\n' sequence with a single space, then replace every remaining '\\n' and every remaining '\\r' with a single space (so 'Line1\\r\\nLine2' becomes 'Line1 Line2' with ONE space between the words; see the worked example further below); STATUS is the task status verbatim when it is one of done|pending|failed else '?'; ATTEMPTS is str(task['retry_count']) when the key exists, else '0'; DEPS is ', '.join(dependencies) when dependencies is a non-empty list, else '-'. Worked example: format_task_row({'id': 'X\\nY', 'title': 'Line1\\r\\nLine2'}) must return exactly 'X Y | Line1 Line2 | ? | 0 | -' (five columns joined by ' | '; empty DEPS renders as '-'). Add parse_diagnosis(feedback: str | None) -> dict | None: only feedback that starts with 'DIAGNOSIS:' AND matches 'DIAGNOSIS: <cause> (confidence=<confidence>) remedy=<remedy>' returns {'cause': str, 'confidence': str, 'remedy': str} (confidence is the raw token after 'confidence='); anything else, including None and 'DIAGNOSIS:' text without the grammar, returns None. Add render_table(projects: list) -> str consuming load_projects' output (list of (name, board-or-exception) tuples; a board is a dict): skip (name, exception) tuples silently; for each readable board emit header '== <name> ==', one format_task_row line per task in board['tasks'] order (a board without a tasks list renders the header only), then one indented line '  DIAGNOSIS: <cause> (confidence=<confidence>) remedy=<remedy>' per task whose 'last_feedback' parses via parse_diagnosis; join all lines with '\\n' and no trailing newline; empty input returns ''. Keep load_projects EXACTLY as given above. No network; stdlib only.",
      "target_files": [
        "src/boardscan.py"
      ],
      "allow_test_edits": false,
      "dependencies": [
        "T-DATALOADER"
      ],
      "priority": "medium",
