      "objective": "Extend src/boardscan.py KEEPING load_projects, format_task_row, parse_diagnosis and render_table unchanged. Add main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int with argparse flags [--root PATH] [--project NAME] [--json]: print render_table(load_projects(root, project)) to stdout and return 0 for a normal run (an empty projects dir prints nothing and returns 0); when any project's board was unreadable, print one line per such project to stderr containing the project name and return 1 AFTER printing the other projects; SystemExit(2) from load_projects (missing root, unknown --project) propagates uncaught; argparse errors exit 2 via argparse itself. --json prints json.dumps(payload, indent=2) of an array over the READABLE projects only, each element {'project': name, 'tasks': [{'id','title','status','retry_count','dependencies'} in board order with status verbatim], 'diagnoses': [{'task_id','cause','confidence','remedy','raw'} per well-formed diagnosis, raw = the full feedback string]} -- unreadable boards stay on stderr and still force return 1. Finish with if __name__ == '__main__': raise SystemExit(main()). No network; stdlib only. Do not change earlier functions.",
